From: Christoph Hellwig <hch@lst.de>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 06:55:58 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] zloop: fix block size query
References: bsc#1012628
Patch-mainline: 7.3.6
Git-commit: 8fbee85a90789d367c347b1cfd5a5ef37f3a934a

commit 8fbee85a90789d367c347b1cfd5a5ef37f3a934a upstream.

The block size obviously needs to be queried when it is not set, not when
it already is set.

Reported: Damien Le Moal <dlemoal@kernel.org>
Fixes: 5e9929e2f03c ("zloop: share more code for opening a zone backing file")
Signed-off-by: Christoph Hellwig <hch@lst.de>
Reviewed-by: Damien Le Moal <dlemoal@kernel.org>
Link: https://patch.msgid.link/20261102055558.3212814-1-hch@lst.de
Signed-off-by: Jens Axboe <axboe@kernel.dk>
Signed-off-by: Greg Kroah-Hartman <gregkh@linuxfoundation.org>
Signed-off-by: Jiri Slaby <jslaby@suse.cz>
---
 drivers/block/zloop.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/block/zloop.c b/drivers/block/zloop.c
index 2933f6db4fd0..e02a5249ae60 100644
--- a/drivers/block/zloop.c
+++ b/drivers/block/zloop.c
@@ -1127,7 +1127,7 @@ static int zloop_init_zone(struct zloop_device *zlo, struct zloop_options *opts,
 		goto out_fput;
 	}
 
-	if (zlo->block_size) {
+	if (!zlo->block_size) {
 		ret = zloop_get_block_size(zlo, zone);
 		if (ret)
 			goto out_fput;
-- 
2.56.1

